WEBVTT

00:16.710 --> 00:20.960
Known as the Blade Dragon 
and Unparalleled in Eight Provinces,

00:20.960 --> 00:24.670
when I stopped finding men stronger than me,

00:26.200 --> 00:30.730
a lord named Something-or-Other Tatsumi 
asked me to become his officer.

00:31.820 --> 00:34.980
He was a great man who took 
pride in his great mansion.

00:34.980 --> 00:39.140
His name's characters made him a "dragon" too,
so I agreed, in exchange for room and board.

00:40.090 --> 00:43.620
You sure can put them back.

00:43.620 --> 00:45.620
Splendid.

00:47.740 --> 00:53.240
Anyway, Tamiya Gantetsusai-dono, 
you may be the Blade Dragon,

00:53.240 --> 00:56.460
but surely you can't kill a real dragon.

00:57.280 --> 00:58.120
What?

00:59.810 --> 01:07.000
So I cut down both the dragon on his gate 
and that cowardly dragon's nerve.

01:08.130 --> 01:11.500
Your temper is too violent. 
I don't understand you.

01:12.660 --> 01:14.140
I agree.

01:14.440 --> 01:17.880
Because of that, his whole clan came 
after me, and I was sentenced to death.

01:17.880 --> 01:19.970
Not that I regret it.

01:20.380 --> 01:23.540
Once I acquire the pardon, 
I'll be cleared of all charges.

01:23.540 --> 01:25.650
Then I can openly hone my skill again.

01:26.080 --> 01:28.650
This time, I'll split his 
whole mansion in half.

01:29.540 --> 01:31.870
I don't understand you.

01:32.140 --> 01:35.430
If you ask me, you people 
make even less sense.

01:35.800 --> 01:38.990
Those tools you're wearing are 
for dissections, aren't they?

01:39.460 --> 01:41.210
What a gloomy little man.

01:41.520 --> 01:45.440
Does the food you earn beheading 
criminals taste good, Whatever-emon?

01:46.370 --> 01:50.240
It's Asaemon. Yamada Asaemon Fuchi.

01:48.590 --> 01:50.970
<b>Tameshi-itto-ryu Rank 9
Yamada Asaemon
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFuchi</b>

01:51.210 --> 01:53.880
Beheadings aren't 
the Yamada clan's only trade.

01:53.880 --> 01:56.170
We also test swords and produce medicines.

01:56.170 --> 01:59.640
We're far more useful to society than you.

02:00.380 --> 02:02.150
The same goes for the dissections.

02:02.150 --> 02:05.480
Discoveries about the human 
body help advance medicine.

02:05.480 --> 02:07.000
It's a noble purpose.

02:13.760 --> 02:15.740
I won't allow you to insult us.

02:19.750 --> 02:21.570
Whatever.

02:21.570 --> 02:23.800
Try not to get in my way.

02:22.140 --> 02:23.800
H-Hey, wait.

02:26.990 --> 02:28.510
Do you know what you're doing?

02:29.110 --> 02:30.880
There's only one thing to do.

02:30.880 --> 02:33.760
I'm going to eliminate the competition.

02:34.510 --> 02:38.300
It's more efficient to take my time 
searching for the Elixir after that,

02:38.300 --> 02:41.030
and most importantly, I can use 
my sword to my heart's content.

02:41.580 --> 02:43.560
I thought I'd never get the chance to

02:43.560 --> 02:47.200
engage in thrilling duels 
in this peaceful world again.

02:48.960 --> 02:50.570
<i>It makes sense.</i>

02:51.320 --> 02:54.100
<i>This job is like crafting insect poison.</i>

02:54.100 --> 02:58.080
<i>The longer you wait, the stronger 
the surviving venomous insects.</i>

02:58.320 --> 03:01.200
<i>But will this really end well?</i>

03:01.710 --> 03:04.080
<i>Not all of the venomous insects are here.</i>

03:04.570 --> 03:08.880
<i>If the shogunate runs out of patience, 
they'll send the next batch of insects.</i>

03:08.880 --> 03:13.080
<i>Stronger, more venomous insects.</i>

03:33.640 --> 03:35.110
Interesting...

03:47.340 --> 03:48.520
Stay back.

05:19.500 --> 05:26.470
<b>Hell and Paradise</b>

05:22.300 --> 05:24.810
<i>What is this thing, a fish?</i>

05:25.110 --> 05:26.720
<i>It's wearing prayer beads.</i>

05:26.720 --> 05:28.880
<i>Is it a monster or a living creature?</i>

05:29.160 --> 05:32.360
<i>Its appearance is ridiculously fantastical.</i>

05:32.360 --> 05:34.400
<i>I have so many questions,</i>

05:34.940 --> 05:38.810
<i>but my instincts are telling me 
that this island itself is dangerous.</i>

05:40.060 --> 05:41.440
<i>What a pain in the butt.</i>

05:52.680 --> 05:53.330
Gabima—

05:57.000 --> 05:58.840
I told you to stay back.

05:58.840 --> 05:59.930
Right.

06:00.550 --> 06:02.730
It seems to be alive.

06:03.790 --> 06:07.130
<i>Shinobi Rule Number Five.</i>

06:07.130 --> 06:11.560
<i>Do not fight an unknown enemy.</i>

06:13.920 --> 06:14.950
<i>Should we run?</i>

06:16.470 --> 06:19.040
<i>The two of us, or just me?</i>

06:31.450 --> 06:34.050
Gabimaru! Are you all right?

06:34.710 --> 06:36.180
<i>This place is dangerous.</i>

06:37.580 --> 06:39.980
So it's possible for you to be injured...

06:39.980 --> 06:41.100
No, wait. I mean—

06:41.640 --> 06:42.720
Let's run for now.

06:52.280 --> 06:53.200
<i>What are they?</i>

06:54.810 --> 06:55.970
<i>They're smiling?</i>

06:56.320 --> 06:58.600
<i>Are they real?</i>

06:59.730 --> 07:03.560
<i>Calm down. Don't lose your head.</i>

07:04.080 --> 07:05.490
We've been surrounded.

07:10.040 --> 07:13.380
<i>Enough. Stop thinking.</i>

07:15.580 --> 07:16.800
Gabimaru!

07:20.970 --> 07:22.720
Ninpo: Ascetic Blaze.

07:30.430 --> 07:31.830
<i>For now, don't think.</i>

07:37.060 --> 07:38.200
<i>Just kill.</i>

07:40.930 --> 07:42.320
<i>So you can survive.</i>

07:42.920 --> 07:46.660
<i>So you can acquire the pardon 
and escape this bloody world.</i>

07:47.710 --> 07:48.950
<i>Just kill.</i>

07:50.530 --> 07:53.400
<i>I knew this was a dangerous job, 
but it's different now.</i>

07:54.900 --> 08:02.500
<i>Everything has changed since mere hours ago.</i>

08:09.190 --> 08:11.680
<i>What an otherworldly sight.</i>

08:12.820 --> 08:16.230
<i>Am I in Paradise, or...?</i>

08:30.400 --> 08:32.320
<i>Don't worry about anything else.</i>

08:32.960 --> 08:34.770
<i>That's not weakness.</i>

08:35.670 --> 08:37.730
<i>Just focus on the enemies in front of you.</i>

08:37.730 --> 08:40.590
<i>True courage is being true to your emotions.</i>

08:40.590 --> 08:41.790
Eliminate them.

08:53.320 --> 08:55.760
Um, Gabimaru...

08:57.120 --> 08:58.060
I'm so—

09:02.610 --> 09:06.270
Wow, you killed all of these by yourself?

09:06.270 --> 09:07.840
Impressive, Hollow!

09:07.840 --> 09:10.780
Wow, that was something else.

09:10.780 --> 09:12.480
Wow.

09:12.480 --> 09:13.950
I'm Yuzuriha.

09:13.950 --> 09:16.160
Like you, I'm a ninja.

09:16.160 --> 09:17.820
We're, like, totally the same.

09:18.240 --> 09:20.500
Two executioners?

09:20.500 --> 09:21.770
What do you think you're...

09:22.730 --> 09:26.860
You're supposed to say "thank you" 
when someone helps you.

09:29.400 --> 09:32.470
Thank you for saving me.

09:33.780 --> 09:38.100
So, what do you want? We're rivals.

09:38.100 --> 09:40.040
You didn't have to help me.

09:41.850 --> 09:44.240
Don't be so on edge.

09:44.240 --> 09:46.360
The monsters are gone now.

09:46.360 --> 09:48.750
You seem super dependable, Gabi-kun.

09:48.750 --> 09:51.580
You're still standing, despite 
how much you're bleeding.

09:51.580 --> 09:54.280
Didn't you save her just now, too?

09:58.010 --> 10:01.510
Hey, why don't we work together?

10:01.840 --> 10:06.710
I'm so scared of this dangerous place.

10:06.710 --> 10:10.270
I'll do whatever you say. Please protect—

10:10.580 --> 10:12.730
Huh? What?

10:12.730 --> 10:14.510
Ow... Ow...

10:14.510 --> 10:18.280
Ow, that hurts! What are you doing?

10:18.280 --> 10:19.910
You can't seduce me.

10:19.910 --> 10:21.650
I'm familiar with kunoichi methods.

10:23.150 --> 10:26.030
Yeah, yeah. I'm sure you are.

10:26.030 --> 10:27.840
I just wanted to try it.

10:27.840 --> 10:30.680
It's better to regret what you've done 
than regret what you haven't, right?

10:31.350 --> 10:34.280
But I'm serious about working together.

10:34.280 --> 10:37.020
Five is safer than three.

10:37.020 --> 10:38.900
Wait a minute.

10:38.900 --> 10:41.300
Why do you have two Asaemon with you?

10:41.720 --> 10:44.430
This guy is, uh...

10:44.430 --> 10:46.470
Yamada Asaemon Genji.

10:46.210 --> 10:47.450
<b>Tameshi-itto-ryu Rank 8
Yamada Asaemon
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hGenji</b>

10:46.470 --> 10:50.680
I was originally assigned 
to Moro Makiya the Apostate.

10:51.120 --> 10:54.180
<i>Makiya died when he was 
fooled by this woman.</i>

10:54.440 --> 10:56.950
Her foul tricks run contrary to bushido.

10:56.950 --> 11:00.760
I deemed a single executioner 
insufficient to control her,

11:01.150 --> 11:03.560
so I decided to accompany them.

11:03.960 --> 11:05.330
Huh.

11:05.330 --> 11:06.860
<i>So she seduced him.</i>

11:06.860 --> 11:08.210
I see.

11:08.210 --> 11:10.680
<i>Women have always been 
Genji-dono's weakness.</i>

11:10.680 --> 11:11.690
<i>He fell for her tricks.</i>

11:13.780 --> 11:14.950
Uh, um...

11:15.330 --> 11:18.980
I'm Yamada Asaemon Senta, 
the executioner assigned to her.

11:18.870 --> 11:20.360
<b>Tameshi-itto-ryu Rank 5
Yamada Asaemon
Senta</b>

11:18.980 --> 11:20.730
Well, you know.

11:20.730 --> 11:26.080
We ran into crazy bugs, monsters, 
statues on our way here.

11:26.080 --> 11:28.720
We know just how dangerous this place is.

11:28.720 --> 11:32.000
Finding the Elixir as quickly 
as possible is important,

11:32.000 --> 11:35.220
but there's no point in blindly 
charging in and dying without a plan.

11:35.520 --> 11:38.280
You're the one who called me disappointing.

11:38.290 --> 11:41.360
Did I? I don't remember that.

11:41.730 --> 11:44.390
As long as you both agree to it,

11:44.400 --> 11:46.330
then there's no problem 
with you working together.

11:46.330 --> 11:48.740
All right! I love you, Gabimaru.

11:48.740 --> 11:51.310
Ow, ow, ow! What are you doing?

11:51.310 --> 11:52.800
I never said I'd work with you.

11:52.800 --> 11:54.240
I can't trust a kunoichi.

11:55.570 --> 11:57.900
Trust? Come on.

11:57.900 --> 11:59.360
We're not kids.

12:03.600 --> 12:05.830
We can betray each other at any time.

12:06.430 --> 12:10.420
Even if we find the Elixir, 
only one of us will be pardoned.

12:10.420 --> 12:13.340
I'm suggesting we use each other 
for as long as possible.

12:13.660 --> 12:16.560
Or are you scared of me?

12:17.030 --> 12:18.220
You're surprisingly naïve.

12:21.260 --> 12:22.940
Please, Gabi.

12:22.940 --> 12:25.150
Won't you help a weak little girl?

12:25.150 --> 12:27.400
You're wasting your time with that.

12:27.400 --> 12:28.520
Oh?

12:29.270 --> 12:31.280
How would working with you benefit me?

12:32.140 --> 12:35.780
You'll offer your strength 
in exchange for my information.

12:36.130 --> 12:37.910
For example,

12:37.910 --> 12:40.590
you seem to think the monsters are a threat,

12:40.590 --> 12:43.300
but the real danger here is the bugs.

12:43.680 --> 12:45.210
Human-faced butterflies.

12:45.450 --> 12:49.430
They fly around monsters, 
but their nests and behavior are unknown.

12:49.770 --> 12:53.320
Their scales seem to contain 
hallucinogens and poison.

12:53.320 --> 12:55.430
How do you know that?

12:58.120 --> 12:59.600
Moro Makiya.

12:59.600 --> 13:02.220
I got close to him and talked him into it.

13:02.220 --> 13:04.140
I tested them on him.

13:04.140 --> 13:07.030
The centipedes are gross, 
but you can safely ignore them.

13:07.030 --> 13:08.910
They only eat dead flesh.

13:08.910 --> 13:10.510
How do you know that?

13:10.510 --> 13:12.280
I tested it on Makiya.

13:12.280 --> 13:16.770
There are other bugs too, 
but they didn't attack unless approached.

13:16.770 --> 13:18.230
I tested it on Makiya.

13:18.500 --> 13:20.290
What happened to him?

13:20.620 --> 13:23.800
I got him to let his guard down 
by playing dead and killed him.

13:23.800 --> 13:31.530
Many of the items worn by the 
monsters feature Buddhist or Taoist designs.

13:31.540 --> 13:34.480
Buddhism and Taoism are 
different religious traditions...

13:34.480 --> 13:37.040
It's strange to see them mixed together.

13:37.040 --> 13:39.320
The Buddhist statues are strange, too.

13:39.320 --> 13:43.800
I have trouble believing 
this island is truly Paradise.

13:43.800 --> 13:45.410
I agree.

13:46.120 --> 13:48.680
We can explain it away 
by calling them fantastical,

13:48.680 --> 13:51.830
but to my blade, their anatomy and musculature

13:51.830 --> 13:53.440
feels like those of living creatures.

13:53.440 --> 13:56.390
See? There's so much we don't know.

13:56.390 --> 13:59.440
We should work together 
and gather information.

13:59.440 --> 14:02.440
I'll tell you everything I know.

14:03.320 --> 14:05.580
Why are you willing to reveal so much?

14:05.580 --> 14:07.640
Are you that desperate to survive?

14:09.720 --> 14:12.330
I have one younger sister.

14:13.110 --> 14:16.830
She's got an incurable disease, 
but can't afford any medicine.

14:17.550 --> 14:20.510
I became a shinobi in order to make money.

14:20.730 --> 14:23.440
I endured hellish training 
with the Kai of Kasumidani.

14:23.440 --> 14:25.110
The Kai shinobi are from Mizoredani.

14:25.110 --> 14:27.140
Uh, right. That place.

14:27.430 --> 14:32.120
Anyway, uh... the village chief, uh...

14:32.120 --> 14:34.470
He said something about 
how I couldn't do that.

14:34.850 --> 14:36.360
And then they betrayed me.

14:36.360 --> 14:38.780
If you're lying, then keep it short.

14:38.780 --> 14:41.160
Oh, you figured it out?

14:41.160 --> 14:44.880
Do I need a reason to want to survive?

14:45.170 --> 14:48.240
Some deep personal motivation?

14:48.670 --> 14:50.690
I've got nothing like that.

14:51.020 --> 14:54.290
Do I need a reason to want to 
make it back home alive?

14:54.290 --> 14:56.880
I don't want to die 
while I'm still so young.

14:57.200 --> 14:58.210
That's all.

14:58.570 --> 15:02.150
Maybe you samurai wouldn't understand.

15:02.150 --> 15:05.840
After all, you risk your lives 
just because the shogun wills it,

15:05.840 --> 15:08.520
and never even question it.

15:09.260 --> 15:12.280
I have another question.

15:12.280 --> 15:12.900
Hmm?

15:13.580 --> 15:17.690
What did you actually do to Moro Makiya?

15:22.160 --> 15:24.650
Nothing.

15:25.170 --> 15:28.250
You care about the lives of others?

15:28.850 --> 15:31.160
It'll get you killed.

15:33.600 --> 15:34.880
Fine.

15:34.880 --> 15:36.960
I want information.

15:36.960 --> 15:39.260
As long as we're simply fighting together 
and not fully cooperating...

15:39.260 --> 15:41.520
All right! You're the best, Gabi-chan.

15:41.520 --> 15:44.470
Ow, ow, ow! I just got a little excited.

15:44.470 --> 15:45.760
What is this for?

15:45.760 --> 15:47.270
I have a wife.

15:47.490 --> 15:49.520
Then let's share what we know.

15:49.520 --> 15:52.480
No, wait. We're working together now.

15:52.480 --> 15:54.270
We don't have to tell them anything else.

15:54.600 --> 15:57.680
The words were barely out of your mouth 
before you went back on them.

15:57.680 --> 16:00.190
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.

16:01.120 --> 16:05.150
<i>What have I done 
since arriving on this island?</i>

16:06.470 --> 16:10.040
<i>I lost my bearings against those monsters 
and let the situation overwhelm me.</i>

16:10.720 --> 16:14.630
<i>What purpose have 
the sword skills I honed served?</i>

16:15.200 --> 16:18.120
<i>I'm so powerless.</i>

16:26.080 --> 16:28.180
<i>Change is strength.</i>

16:29.980 --> 16:32.620
He became an agent of the clan 
within a month of joining it.

16:32.620 --> 16:34.310
Impressive, Toma.

16:34.670 --> 16:38.740
The final step is for you to execute a 
criminal so we can add your name to the list.

16:38.740 --> 16:40.800
Which execution would be suitable?

16:43.500 --> 16:45.470
I have a request.

16:52.320 --> 16:53.880
Thank you for waiting.

16:54.400 --> 16:56.680
I've come to save you, brother.

16:57.500 --> 16:59.430
Took you long enough.

16:59.430 --> 17:02.290
Not even a word of thanks 
for your younger brother who infiltrated

17:02.290 --> 17:04.590
the Yamada clan and achieved 
this status within a month?

17:04.780 --> 17:08.570
I endured a month of torture at their hands.

17:08.570 --> 17:10.840
And now you're more handsome than ever.

17:10.840 --> 17:12.840
So, how are we getting out?

17:12.840 --> 17:14.980
The magistrate's men don't give up easily.

17:15.640 --> 17:19.240
There's apparently a way 
to make them stop pursing us.

17:21.090 --> 17:22.560
I'm in.

17:22.860 --> 17:26.480
<i>Change means changing yourself 
according to the situation.</i>

17:27.420 --> 17:28.600
Brother...

17:28.600 --> 17:31.990
<i>Quickly appraising a situation 
and understanding it.</i>

17:31.990 --> 17:34.870
Are these things alive?

17:34.870 --> 17:38.010
<i>Some situations can be 
difficult to understand.</i>

17:41.070 --> 17:43.640
Then they can be killed!

17:43.640 --> 17:47.370
<i>My brother's strength is 
how quickly he understands situations.</i>

17:47.840 --> 17:49.310
<i>He always has.</i>

17:49.980 --> 17:54.600
<i>Even when the lord our father 
served committed an outrage</i>

17:51.730 --> 17:54.600
A lord's crimes are his vassals' crimes!

17:54.600 --> 17:57.230
<i>at Edo Castle and our clan was disbanded.</i>

17:59.630 --> 18:02.670
<i>Even when our mother died 
while we were living in poverty.</i>

18:03.800 --> 18:09.490
For avenging their master, 
all 47 ronin shall be beheaded.

18:10.710 --> 18:15.080
<i>Even when our father was executed 
for avenging his lord.</i>

18:23.510 --> 18:25.800
<i>Even when we were attacked by bandits.</i>

18:26.180 --> 18:31.840
<i>He immediately understood the situation 
and ultimately ended up controlling it.</i>

18:32.300 --> 18:35.180
Give yourself up, Bandit King Chobe!

18:35.470 --> 18:37.930
Come quietly!

18:38.340 --> 18:40.790
Toma, I want you to run.

18:40.790 --> 18:41.500
Brother.

18:41.500 --> 18:43.320
Come rescue me later.

18:44.380 --> 18:46.320
I believe in you.

18:48.810 --> 18:51.990
<i>We don't live in a world 
where the strong prey on the weak.</i>

18:52.510 --> 18:54.130
<i>It's survival of the fittest.</i>

18:54.130 --> 18:56.490
<i>It's those who can adapt that are strong.</i>

19:00.830 --> 19:02.150
Brother...

19:00.830 --> 19:02.150
Toma,

19:02.150 --> 19:03.950
we're slipping through the monsters.

19:03.950 --> 19:05.080
Got it.

19:06.340 --> 19:10.120
<i>Fleeing a situation you can't 
understand can also be the right choice.</i>

19:11.280 --> 19:13.380
<i>My brother is a genius when it comes to change.</i>

19:14.230 --> 19:16.720
<i>The one thing that hasn't changed is...</i>

19:22.670 --> 19:24.100
Brother...

19:28.130 --> 19:30.260
<i>Change is strength.</i>

19:32.440 --> 19:36.740
<i>Those who cannot change are unnecessary.</i>

19:37.750 --> 19:41.860
<i>That's why my brother is strong.</i>

19:43.280 --> 19:44.720
Damn monsters!

19:44.720 --> 19:46.620
You won't get past me!

19:52.880 --> 19:56.540
What's more effective against a monster 
than its own weapons?

19:56.540 --> 19:57.600
Brother...

19:57.600 --> 20:01.480
You bought me time to pick up a weapon.

20:03.580 --> 20:04.670
Brother!

20:05.720 --> 20:08.440
Brother! Brother! Brother! Brother!

20:11.590 --> 20:13.520
Murder is a sin.

20:15.670 --> 20:18.310
Even insects are alive.

20:18.310 --> 20:20.050
So are fish.

20:20.050 --> 20:22.040
You mustn't harm them.

20:20.800 --> 20:22.930
These things can talk?

20:22.040 --> 20:24.400
Murder is a sin.

20:23.390 --> 20:27.050
Brother, are these real deities?

20:27.670 --> 20:31.180
Are we in not in Heaven, 
but in Hell instead?

20:31.760 --> 20:34.480
Where sinners receive divine punishment?

20:37.880 --> 20:40.830
A lord's crimes are his vassals' crimes!

20:40.830 --> 20:42.260
They shall be executed!

20:42.260 --> 20:44.930
Arrest that criminal Chobe!

20:47.240 --> 20:51.690
I'm sick of hearing about crimes and sins.

20:53.690 --> 20:55.320
Evil? Sin?

20:55.320 --> 20:56.950
I don't give a shit.

20:56.950 --> 20:59.080
You're the ones who decided that.

20:59.570 --> 21:02.450
You're slaves to righteousness.

21:02.450 --> 21:05.580
You're puppets without your own desires.

21:06.150 --> 21:08.720
I'm not letting anyone 
else tell me what to do.

21:08.720 --> 21:11.470
I'll do what I wanna do.

21:13.290 --> 21:15.560
I'm my own lord.

21:15.930 --> 21:18.910
I'm my own <i>god</i>.

21:19.440 --> 21:21.810
<i>My brother's strength is change.</i>

21:21.810 --> 21:26.070
<i>And because he changes, 
it always comes to the fore...</i>

21:26.440 --> 21:28.800
<i>His unyielding sense of self.</i>

21:29.390 --> 21:32.320
Father, Mother...

21:32.820 --> 21:35.320
I wanna go back to the mansion.

21:36.170 --> 21:39.400
We were the sons of samurai, 
but now we're bandits.

21:40.330 --> 21:45.330
I don't know what's right anymore.

21:50.840 --> 21:52.520
Don't cry, Toma.

21:52.520 --> 21:54.460
Show any weakness, and you'll die.

21:54.460 --> 21:57.720
If you don't know what's right, then trust me.

21:58.100 --> 21:59.720
I'm your older brother.

21:59.720 --> 22:02.160
An older brother shows his 
younger brother the way.

22:02.160 --> 22:04.160
I'm always right.

22:07.750 --> 22:12.230
If these monsters exist, 
then the Elixir must be real as well.

22:12.760 --> 22:14.000
All right.

22:14.390 --> 22:15.490
I've made up my mind.

22:15.490 --> 22:18.920
We'll kill every last monster and criminal.

22:18.920 --> 22:22.230
Then no one can stop us 
from finding the Elixir.

22:22.230 --> 22:25.300
We'll drink the Elixir ourselves.

22:25.630 --> 22:31.240
Not even death will be 
able to tell us how to live.

22:35.160 --> 22:37.660
Will it really go so well?

22:37.660 --> 22:38.460
What?

22:38.910 --> 22:40.970
This island is a dangerous place.

22:41.220 --> 22:45.730
Anyone else we meet will be another survivor.

22:46.170 --> 22:48.980
The threats here are that great.

22:50.240 --> 22:53.130
The weak will be weeded out.

22:53.130 --> 22:55.130

